{
  "_about": "Overlay for what the authored transport files do not say. The region transport JSON only links place to place, so a destination whose guide says 'arrive at NJP station or Bagdogra airport' (Gangtok) had no train in the quote, and a trip had no notion of where the traveller actually enters the region. This file adds: hubs (the airports and stations a traveller really arrives at), railheads (the practical station for a place), portSubstitutes (airports with too little scheduled service to be a port of entry, replaced by the main one), hillStates (road speeds there are about half the plains figure), and roadHops (the real road from a hub to a place where the distance model is wrong). Add a row here, run `npm run build-atlas` or just reload; nothing else needs regenerating.",
